.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt REALPATH 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm realpath
.Nd write resolved pathnames
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl q
.Op Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes, for each
.Ar path ,
the absolute pathname of the file it names, with every symbolic link
followed and no
.Pa \&. ,
.Pa ..
or extra
.Ql /
left, as
.Xr realpath 3
makes it.
With no
.Ar path ,
the working directory's.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl q
Say nothing about a
.Ar path
that can't be resolved, such as one that doesn't exist (the exit status
still says so).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl realpath /usr/../etc/./rc
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pwd 1 ,
.Xr readlink 1 ,
.Xr realpath 3
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.Fx 4.3 .
